{"kind":"driver:amendment","task":"2","amends":"clause","what":"M1's `a driver:wave-blocked event whose fold ended CONFLICT carries paths` — read as carrying the receipt only when that epoch narrated at least one path, so a CONFLICT whose conflicts.json is empty or absent emits neither `paths` nor `evidence`. Same narrowing in `foldReceiptOf`: it also returns null when `open` is non-empty but no row carries a `path` string.","why":"The Context's RECEIPT SHAPE, the shared literal of the plan, says `paths` is never empty, and M2 gives the rationale outright — a fold that conflicted on no path names no file, and a receipt names files. Emitting `paths: []` would have broken the shape every other task of the plan reads. No Proof leg covers that case either way; legs (a) and (b) are unaffected.","id":"01M2MK154H0000T9QXY29XEKMZ","ts":1789544928401}
